 Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"eba51142a1a4fbba","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"59fb1e0759e1f869","name":"Demand Surrender","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisites":"Farseeing","benefit":"Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can remove one ongoing Mind-Affecting effect (such as the effects of or Weaken Resolve Talents, or the effect of being moved to the end of the Condition Track by the Adept Negotiator Talent, or the ongoing effects of the Mind Trick Force Power) from a single allied target within line of sight. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide When you use Farseeing, or a Force Power or Talent that has Farseeing as a prerequisite, other Force-users with Farseeing in their Force Power Suite can Aid Another on your Use the Force check as a Reaction, if they are within 6 squares of you. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Once per round as a Swift Action, you grant one ally within 12 squares of you (and within your line of sight) Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + your Charisma modifier. These Bonus Hit Points last until the beginning of your next turn (at which point any remaining Bonus Hit Points are lost), and any damage dealt to that ally comes out of Bonus Hit Points first. You take a -5 penalty on all Use the Force checks until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide","description":"Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can remove one ongoing Mind-Affecting effect (such as the effects of or Weaken Resolve Talents, or the effect of being moved to the end of the Condition Track by the Adept Negotiator Talent, or the ongoing effects of the Mind Trick Force Power) from a single allied target within line of sight. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide When you use Farseeing, or a Force Power or Talent that has Farseeing as a prerequisite, other Force-users with Farseeing in their Force Power Suite can Aid Another on your Use the Force check as a Reaction, if they are within 6 squares of you. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Once per round as a Swift Action, you grant one ally within 12 squares of you (and within your line of sight) Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + your Charisma modifier. These Bonus Hit Points last until the beginning of your next turn (at which point any remaining Bonus Hit Points are lost), and any damage dealt to that ally comes out of Bonus Hit Points first. You take a -5 penalty on all Use the Force checks until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","light-side","mobility","noble","positioning","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.demand_surrender"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.871638a983029bc4"}}},{"_id":"25b813dd3032cce4","name":"Hyperdriven","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Once per day, add your class level to an attack, skill, or ability check.","description":"Once per day, add your class level to an attack roll, skill check, or ability check.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["scoundrel","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hyperdriven"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.29f73c36cabdeaf5"}}},{"_id":"d9cce17de338adff","name":"Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec8f2ba706cc2c05"}}},{"_id":"aa809d34c06f2568","name":"Spacehound","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","description":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["action-economy","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","shields","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spacehound"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fe0c3a64ca460542"}}},{"_id":"caba52fae7640361","name":"Starship Raider","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":"Spacehound","benefit":"+1 attack aboard starships, including with personal weapons.","description":"Gain +1 attack aboard starships with personal weapons.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.spacehound"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["feat-chain","scoundrel","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"e4be147d-37ec-4006-90a5-976c3d591ef7","name":"Starship Raider","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Starship Raider"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.starship_raider"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.224906e573330bf2"}}},{"_id":"31483f7c8a8caeab","name":"Vehicular Evasion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you Fly Defensively as the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may negate a weapon hit on your Vehicle using the Vehicular Combat feat one additional time per round. Once per encounter, when a Vehicle you're Piloting takes damage that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, your Vehicle avoids moving down the Condition Track. You may roll twice for any opposed Pilot check made to initiate a Dogfight, keeping the better result. If the Vehicle you are piloting is hit by an Area Attack, it takes half damage if the attack hits. If the Area Attack misses your Vehicle, it takes no damage. You cannot use this Talent when your Vehicle is stationary or disabled. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy You can fly a Vehicle you Pilot so close to a target at least two sizes larger than your Vehicle that it is difficult for the target to avoid or attack you. You must be adjacent to the target (at Starship Scale) to use this Talent.","description":"When you Fly Defensively as the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may negate a weapon hit on your Vehicle using the Vehicular Combat feat one additional time per round. Once per encounter, when a Vehicle you're Piloting takes damage that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, your Vehicle avoids moving down the Condition Track. You may roll twice for any opposed Pilot check made to initiate a Dogfight, keeping the better result. If the Vehicle you are piloting is hit by an Area Attack, it takes half damage if the attack hits. If the Area Attack misses your Vehicle, it takes no damage. You cannot use this Talent when your Vehicle is stationary or disabled. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy You can fly a Vehicle you Pilot so close to a target at least two sizes larger than your Vehicle that it is difficult for the target to avoid or attack you. You must be adjacent to the target (at Starship Scale) to use this Talent.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Expert Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["battlefield-control","condition-removal","controller","defender","evasion","mechanics","piloting","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"5929f21c-82c9-4c5d-b26a-a056bd79bd7c","name":"Vehicular Evasion","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.vehicles.damage_reduction","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Vehicular Evasion"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vehicular_evasion"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f0cf0ad742a5e014"}}},{"_id":"c12b