atType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with rifles and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"3b695d0d-747b-4081-8b6c-8b5f8584ff43","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"4497b2bf0625691c","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"0134ca1c630d27ea","name":"Battle Analysis","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","description":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Commando","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mechanics","mobility","piloting","positioning","ranged","scaling","shields","skills","social","soldier","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_analysis"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7df2e8e4f18dc909"}}},{"_id":"0b3e0ec9ca59afe9","name":"Devastating Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Weapon Master","prerequisites":"","benefit":"This replaces the effects of the Talent.","description":"This replaces the effects of the Talent.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Weapon Master","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["soldier"]},"effects":[{"_id":"69f7a1a0-603e-4b5e-a42a-15f770230266","name":"Devastating Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.combat.weaponGroupThresholdReduction","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Devastating Attack","effectType":"threshold_reduction","weaponGroupSpecific":true,"notes":"Weapon group specific - applies when using designated weapon group"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.devastating_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.383915a7d11e1225"}}},{"_id":"7cfbc4f67989d883","name":"Dogfight Gunner","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunner","prerequisites":"Expert Gunner","benefit":"No penalty with vehicle weapons even if you are not the pilot.","description":"Suffer no penalties when using vehicle weapons while not piloting.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Gunner","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.expert_gunner"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","tags":["feat-chain","scout","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dogfight_gunner"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f52cadb1ae252d0c"}}},{"_id":"1aaeb6496c872493","name":"Expert Gunner","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunner","prerequisites":"","benefit":"While your Vehicle is engaged in a Dogfight, you take no penalty on your attack rolls with Vehicle Weapons, even if you are not the Pilot. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made using Vehicle Weapons. Prerequisite: Whenever an enemy Vehicle moves out of your square, or an adjacent square, you may make a single attack against that Vehicle as an Attack of Opportunity. Prerequisite: Whenever you deal damage to a Vehicle that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, you move that Vehicle an additional -1 step on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , System Hit Whenever you make an attack that causes a Vehicle to move -1 or more steps down the Condition Track, you may also cause it to lose one of the following systems: Hyperdrive, one Weapon System or Weapon Battery, or communications. The system remains inoperable until the target regains all steps on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Quick Trigger Once per encounter, when Piloting a Vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent one additional time in an encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy When firing a Vehicle Weapon, you treat the distance to the target as though it were one Range category less than it actually is. For example, when targeting an opponent at Short Range, you treat it as though it were at least Point-Blank Range for the purpose of determining bonuses or penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisite: You know how to overcharge your Vehicle's weapon to produce additional damage. As a Swift Action, you can overcharge your Vehicle's energy weapon and deal +1 die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again, until a full round passes without the weapon firing. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, you may ready to fire a single weapon at the same target as an ally, and you coordinate with a single weapon of your ally. If both attacks hit, you add the damage of the two weapons together before applying the target's Shield Rating or Damage Reduction, and treat it as a single attack for purposes of exceeding the target's Damage Threshold.","description":"While your Vehicle is engaged in a Dogfight, you take no penalty on your attack rolls with Vehicle Weapons, even if you are not the Pilot. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made using Vehicle Weapons. Prerequisite: Whenever an enemy Vehicle moves out of your square, or an adjacent square, you may make a single attack against that Vehicle as an Attack of Opportunity. Prerequisite: Whenever you deal damage to a Vehicle that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, you move that Vehicle an additional -1 step on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , System Hit Whenever you make an attack that causes a Vehicle to move -1 or more steps down the Condition Track, you may also cause it to lose one of the following systems: Hyperdrive, one Weapon System or Weapon Battery, or communications. The system remains inoperable until the target regains all steps on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Quick Trigger Once per encounter, when Piloting a Vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent one additional time in an encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy When firing a Vehicle Weapon, you treat the distance to the target as though it were one Range category less than it actually is. For example, when targeting an opponent at Short Range, you treat it as though it were at least Point-Blank Range for the purpose of determining bonuses or penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisite: You know how to overcharge your Vehicle's weapon to produce additional damage. As a Swift Action, you can overcharge your Vehicle's energy weapon and deal +1 die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again, until a full round passes without the weapon firing. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, you may ready to fire a single weapon at the same target as an ally, and you coordinate with a single weapon of your ally. If both attacks hit, you add the damage of the two weapons together before applying the target's Shield Rating or Damage Reduction, and treat it as a single attack for purposes of exceeding the target's Damage Threshold.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Gunner","treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","dual-wield","force","force-control","force-offense","mobility","piloting","positioning","scout","shields","skills","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"19db7346-c8b7-44de-a92a-3a48795e7596","name":"Expert Gunner","icon":"icons/svg/gun.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.ranged","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Expert Gunner"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.expert_gunner"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.befaa195df06b274"}}},{"_id":"42588b8056ba0b29","name":"Penetrating Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Weapon Master","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Chosen Weapon)","benefit":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","description":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Weapon Master","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["feat-chain","leader","scaling","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a0fba2f5-3da6-476e-9ac5-900be2d16e6b","name":"Penetrating Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.combat.weaponGroupDRReduction","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Penetrating Attack","effectType":"dr_reduction","weaponGroupSpecific":true,"notes":"Weapon group specific - applies when using designated weapon group"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.penetrating_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7d547902b8d9109e"}}},{"_id":"ca3ede703fb54995","name":"Relentless Pursuit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":null,"benef