with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"92d3e067e5295184","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with rifles and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"3b695d0d-747b-4081-8b6c-8b5f8584ff43","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"dad500d609627419","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"a3d358403f5a6262","name":"Ambush Specialist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Ambusher","prerequisites":"","benefit":"After you designate a Prime Target, you deal +1 die of damage on attacks against the Prime Target until the end of the encounter. Prerequisite: If you reduce your Prime Target to 0 Hit Points, as a Free Action you can designate another target within your line of sight as your new Prime Target. This new target remains your Prime Target until the end of the encounter. Prerequisite: Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can make an Initiative check, opposed by the Initiative check of your Prime Target. If your check result equals or exceeds your Prime Target's check result, your target is Flat-Footed against all attacks you make before the end of your turn. Prerequisite: You gain a +5 circumstance bonus to Perception checks against your Prime Target until the end of the encounter. If you and all your allies roll higher Initiative checks to start combat than do all your opponents, you automatically gain a Surprise Round, even if the opponents are aware of you when combat begins.","description":"After you designate a Prime Target, you deal +1 die of damage on attacks against the Prime Target until the end of the encounter. Prerequisite: If you reduce your Prime Target to 0 Hit Points, as a Free Action you can designate another target within your line of sight as your new Prime Target. This new target remains your Prime Target until the end of the encounter. Prerequisite: Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can make an Initiative check, opposed by the Initiative check of your Prime Target. If your check result equals or exceeds your Prime Target's check result, your target is Flat-Footed against all attacks you make before the end of your turn. Prerequisite: You gain a +5 circumstance bonus to Perception checks against your Prime Target until the end of the encounter. If you and all your allies roll higher Initiative checks to start combat than do all your opponents, you automatically gain a Surprise Round, even if the opponents are aware of you when combat begins.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Ambusher","treeId":"12027e0ad5e4d260","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","damage-reduction","mobility","perception","scout","skills","soldier","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"55971dae-5cdf-40b0-823d-79482f07dbde","name":"Ambush Specialist","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Ambush Specialist"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ambush_specialist"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e835b21a01ae2ee7"}}},{"_id":"ba38aa3b8e8e528c","name":"Surefooted","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Survivor","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Speed is not reduced by difficult terrain.","description":"Your speed is not reduced by difficult terrain.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Survivor","treeId":"9b06340233eb3cdd","tags":["controller","damage-reduction","mobility","scout"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.surefooted"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f87bd82a892f69ea"}}},{"_id":"102f3ba44449f710","name":"Surveillance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spy","prerequisites":"Trained in Perception","benefit":"Trained in Perception When you successfully use the Talent, you grant yourself and your allies a +1 insight bonus to all Defenses against the target. Prerequisite: Experienced spies and Scouts remember many details from previous assignments, providing insights on later missions. Once per encounter as a Standard Action, you can Take 20 on a check involving a Knowledge skill you are Trained in, or Take 10 on a check involving a Knowledge skill you are Untrained in, even if circumstances would not normally allow you to Take 10 or Take 20. As a Full-Round Action, you can make a Perception check against a single target within line of sight. The DC is equal to 15 or the target's Stealth check result (if the target is actively trying to remain hidden), whichever is greater. If the check is successful, you grant yourself and all allies within line of sight a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against that target until the end of your next turn. Your allies must be able to hear and understand you to benefit from this bonus, and they do not lose the benefit if they move out of line of sight after it is used. Spies specialize in leaving no evidence of their presence when they tamper with advanced electronics or basic mechanical systems. When using Mechanics to Disable Device, you automatically leave no trace when tampering (with no DC increase), and you must fail by 10 or more (instead of 5 or more) before something goes wrong.","description":"Trained in Perception When you successfully use the Talent, you grant yourself and your allies a +1 insight bonus to all Defenses against the target. Prerequisite: Experienced spies and Scouts remember many details from previous assignments, providing insights on later missions. Once per encounter as a Standard Action, you can Take 20 on a check involving a Knowledge skill you are Trained in, or Take 10 on a check involving a Knowledge skill you are Untrained in, even if circumstances would not normally allow you to Take 10 or Take 20. As a Full-Round Action, you can make a Perception check against a single target within line of sight. The DC is equal to 15 or the target's Stealth check result (if the target is actively trying to remain hidden), whichever is greater. If the check is successful, you grant yourself and all allies within line of sight a +2 insight bonus on attack rolls against that target until the end of your next turn. Your allies must be able to hear and understand you to benefit from this bonus, and they do not lose the benefit if they move out of line of sight after it is used. Spies specialize in leaving no evidence of their presence when they tamper with advanced electronics or basic mechanical systems. When using Mechanics to Disable Device, you automatically leave no trace when tampering (with no DC increase), and you must fail by 10 or more (instead of 5 or more) before something goes wrong.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Spy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"43c5941072ec78af"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"7c42882a1347ef18","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","feat-chain","leader","mechanics","mobility","perception","scout","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.surveillance"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f23b63464e0aeff7"}}},{"_id":"5813b377f410dd74","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img"