 do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"3b695d0d-747b-4081-8b6c-8b5f8584ff43","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"2cb8d128bebf7a75","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"6f085c25f8edf421","name":"Damage Reduction 10","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Gain DR 10 for one minute.","description":"Gain damage reduction 10 for one minute.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["defender","force"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a33bfc46-2971-4f80-b25b-3facd242fa76","name":"Damage Reduction 10","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damageReduction","mode":5,"value":"10"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Damage Reduction 10"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.damage_reduction_10"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.35b42e14e3ef7d0d"}}},{"_id":"cc8d9bc0a0fb350a","name":"Devastating Melee Smash","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Brawler","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can attempt a . You must declare this special melee attack before making the attack roll. If the attack rolls succeeds, add half your level to the damage, instead of the normal +1 bonus for the Melee Smash Talent. The damage from this Talent does not stack with any damage bonus provided by the Powerful Charge feat. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue When you successfully Disarm an opponent, you can make an immediate free attack with the disarmed weapon at a -5 penalty. If you are not proficient with the weapon, you take the penalty for nonproficiency as well. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue When Grabbing a target, you take a -2 penalty to your attack roll (instead of the normal -5 penalty). Until the target breaks the Grab, it takes a -5 penalty to attack rolls, including those made with Natural and Light Weapons (instead of the normal -2 penalty). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Once per encounter, you can attempt a . You must declare this special melee attack before making the attack roll. If the attack rolls succeeds, add half your level to the damage, instead of the normal +1 bonus for the Melee Smash Talent. The damage from this Talent does not stack with any damage bonus provided by the Powerful Charge feat. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue When you successfully Disarm an opponent, you can make an immediate free attack with the disarmed weapon at a -5 penalty. If you are not proficient with the weapon, you take the penalty for nonproficiency as well. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue When Grabbing a target, you take a -2 penalty to your attack roll (instead of the normal -5 penalty). Until the target breaks the Grab, it takes a -5 penalty to attack rolls, including those made with Natural and Light Weapons (instead of the normal -2 penalty). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Brawler","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.melee_smash"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67fdd8dce9abd6c1","tags":["melee","mobility","scaling","soldier","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.devastating_melee_smash"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d7e9b15e21ea1c4e"}}},{"_id":"fb5fa84a3427a6ef","name":"Empower Weapon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Item","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can hurl Simple Weapons (Melee), or Advanced Melee Weapons your size or smaller as a Standard Action, treating it as a Thrown Weapon. The Thrown Weapon deals normal weapon damage if it hits. If the weapon deals piercing or slashing damage, it becomes embedded in your target, remaining there and causing an additional die of damage each round at the end of the target's turn, and also when it is removed (removing the embedded weapon is a Swift Action, and an adjacent ally can remove the embedded weapon for you). Your target must be within 6 squares of you. The weapon does not automatically return to you, but you can retrieve it with the Move Object Force Power (dealing an additional die of damage in the process, if the weapon is embedded in the target, as above). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite:","description":"You can hurl Simple Weapons (Melee), or Advanced Melee Weapons your size or smaller as a Standard Action, treating it as a Thrown Weapon. The Thrown Weapon deals normal weapon damage if it hits. If the weapon deals piercing or slashing damage, it becomes embedded in your target, remaining there and causing an additional die of damage each round at the end of the target's turn, and also when it is removed (removing the embedded weapon is a Swift Action, and an adjacent ally can remove the embedded weapon for you). Your target must be within 6 squares of you. The weapon does not automatically return to you, but you can retrieve it with the Move Object Force Power (dealing an additional die of damage in the process, if the weapon is embedded in the target, as above). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite:","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Force Item","treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["action-economy","controller","force","force-control","force-offense","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.empower_weapon"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5218d5971b78119b"}}},{"_id":"66232faad272d6bf","name":"Equilibrium","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Adept","prerequisites":"","benefit":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Force Adept","treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","defender","force","shields","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.equilibrium"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.328a880e60f2320f"}}},{"_id":"1e9c649c9b5fe496","name":"Melee Smash","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Melee Specialist","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Unrelenting Assault You twirl your Weapon around you in a blur, creating a circle of death around you. Any enemy target that begins its turn adjacent to you takes damage equal to your Strength bonus. You must be wielding a Melee Weapon to be using this Talent.","description":"Unrelenting Assault You twirl your Weapon around you in a blur, creating a circle of death around you. Any enemy target that begins its turn adjacent to you takes damage equal to your Strength bonus. You must be wielding a Melee Weapon to be using this Talent.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Melee Specialist","treeId":"fad8118981c532f0","tags":["melee","positioning","soldier","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"2d692811-5c22-48b8-944d-45db89ca5e77","name":"Melee Smash","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.melee","mode":5,"value":"half_level"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Melee Smash"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.melee_smash"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e0ee525f4109cfde"}}},{"_id":"021099872261d8bd","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"c88ff34e17b3f8d0","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"1b8286d32f66b25a","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{