\">Light Armor</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/Medium_Armor\" title=\"Medium Armor\">Medium Armor</a>."}},"effects":[{"_id":"af0983df-e771-4593-8f88-f0aa43612597","name":"Armor Proficiency (Medium)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.armorProficiency.medium","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Armor Proficiency (Medium)","effectType":"armor_proficiency"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.d445051370a88a7f"}}},{"_id":"e76cf6a4c70b769d","name":"Force Sensitivity","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You can make Use the Force checks and gain access to Force Talents.","prerequisite":"Non-Droid","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":86,"tags":["feat-chain","force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"You can make <a href=\"/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> checks and gain access to <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Talents\" title=\"Force Talents\">Force Talents</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ddbeb23013d9e917"}}},{"_id":"0329e93901b359e5","name":"Force Training","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You learn a number of Force powers equal to 1 + your Wisdom modifier.","prerequisite":"Force Sensitivity, Trained in Use the Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Jedi"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"forcePowerGrants":1,"description":{"value":"Learn a number of <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Powers\" title=\"Force Powers\">Force Powers</a> equal to 1 + your <a href=\"/wiki/Wisdom\" title=\"Wisdom\">Wisdom</a> modifier (minimum 1)."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"usetheforce"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[{"_id":"d1c60a9b-78e6-4601-85a4-320794fa5a91","name":"Force Training","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Force Training","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Force Training"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.9b7b869a86f39190"}}},{"_id":"a72e34985304e8db","name":"Martial Arts I","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Increases damage from Unarmed attacks by one die step; gain +1 bonus to Reflex Defense.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":86,"tags":["defender","non-force","striker","unarmed"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Increases damage from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Unarmed\" title=\"Unarmed\">Unarmed</a> attacks by one die step; gain +1 bonus to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Reflex_Defense\" title=\"Reflex Defense\">Reflex Defense</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.92f927c92ded9fcf"}}},{"_id":"c411a0f88cf178da","name":"Skill Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +5 bonus on all checks with the selected skill.","prerequisite":"Trained in the chosen skill","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","noble","non-force","scoundrel","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Noble","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain +5 competence bonus on <a href=\"/wiki/Skill_Checks\" title=\"Skill Checks\">Skill Checks</a> with one <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained_Skill\" title=\"Trained Skill\">Trained Skill</a>."}},"effects":[{"name":"Skill Focus","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.miscMod","mode":2,"value":"5","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"transfer":true,"flags":{"swse":{"type":"skill-bonus","skill":"43c5941072ec78af","source":"Skill Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.1592aaedf4b6e40a"}}},{"_id":"145970190d215977","name":"Strong in the Force","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"Roll d8s instead of d6s when you spend a Force Point.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Roll d8s instead of d6s when you spend a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Force_Point\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.71892687abbed346"}}},{"_id":"639c3198aef703c8","name":"Weapon Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the selected weapon group.","prerequisite":"Proficient with selected weapon group","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"+1 bonus on attack rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"933bbb4d74234c46","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"f2ef70e01ae14d8f","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"35e4664dc45c147a","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with rifles and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"3b695d0d-747b-4081-8b6c-8b5f8584ff43","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"ae2fa1923a5eba78","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"6267d935088e9008","name":"Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Knight's Armor","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"97ac1e99f5213f26","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"ae8bc666d13f6ce1","name":"Force Perception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","description":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","light-side","mobility","scout","skills","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"name":"Force Perception (Trained)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.trained","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Perception","effectType":"skill-trained"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_perception"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a358402a9fc26c02"}}},{"_id":"c064f2c55f3cc630","name":"Gauge Force Potential","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"Force Perception","benefit":"Use the Force vs Will to detect Force sensitivity, number of powers known, and Force Points.","description":"Use the Force to detect Force sensitivity, powers known, and Force Points.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["feat-chain","force","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.gauge_force_potential"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fdc4061afb97e87f"}}},{"_id":"ee3ad24dbe62de61","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"19647358678fe143","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"e3660e39c1d5da1c","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","lightning"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0a422b939edfad56"}}},{"_id":"16af51dab0cf8fe3","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"0c67815118f6e45b","name":"Slow","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Slow"}}},{"_id":"52950b35d66e2610","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d6+6","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":10,"flatDamageFormula":"1d6+6","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"83d9472a83978279","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+9","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":12,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+