,"icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"f00e074a8f890db3","name":"Acute Senses","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Master Scout","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","description":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Master Scout","treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","tags":["action-economy","armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scout","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.acute_senses"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f0166d26d9f6252a"}}},{"_id":"813d8991968dacae","name":"Improved Stealth","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Camouflage","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Camouflage","treeId":"3926d582d2077489","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","mobility","perception","piloting","positioning","ranged","scout","skills","stealth","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_stealth"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.073115894cad8cf9"}}},{"_id":"fe55e6f04810b73a","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+1","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"we