apons and <a href=\"/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a>."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":1}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.252b67d6e31c377e"}}},{"_id":"79f11584cd639db1","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"3cffda8cefecbcc9","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"04e8a8d1d999f928","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"5f3fbd99d0fe2234","name":"Improved Cloak","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You can maintain your Cloak Force Power as a Move Action instead of a Standard Action.","prerequisite":"Cloak","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Clone Wars Campaign Guide","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You can maintain your Cloak Force Power as a Move Action instead of a Standard Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Cloak</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Cloak</p>","relatedPower":"Cloak"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c3feb409cb7b57bf"}}},{"_id":"86d937badac78946","name":"Adept Negotiator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","description":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Consular","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","jedi","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","positioning","scout","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.adept_negotiator"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7acc479dee2d3b10"}}},{"_id":"18ec6370f84b07f7","name":"Channel Aggression","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You let your anger swell into a Rage. As a Swift Action, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Rage bonus on melee attack rolls and melee damage rolls for a number of rounds equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier. At the end of this duration, you move -1 step along the Condition Track. While Raging, you cannot use Skills that require patience and concentration, such as Mechanics, Stealth, or Use the Force. Prerequisite: Whenever you score a Critical Hit, you may spend a Force Point to also reduce the target's Speed by half until they are fully healed (that is, restored to maximum Hit Points). Prerequisites: , Channel Anger Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, you may reroll your Use the Force check, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Upon choosing this Talent, you can no longer use Force Powers with the [Light Side] descriptor. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual","description":"You let your anger swell into a Rage. As a Swift Action, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Rage bonus on melee attack rolls and melee damage rolls for a number of rounds equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier. At the end of this duration, you move -1 step along the Condition Track. While Raging, you cannot use Skills that require patience and concentration, such as Mechanics, Stealth, or Use the Force. Prerequisite: Whenever you score a Critical Hit, you may spend a Force Point to also reduce the target's Speed by half until they are fully healed (that is, restored to maximum Hit Points). Prerequisites: , Channel Anger Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, you may reroll your Use the Force check, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Upon choosing this Talent, you can no longer use Force Powers with the [Light Side] descriptor. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","treeId":"96ef43a3054dcb58","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","force","force-control","force-offense","force-support","light-side","mechanics","medicine","melee","mobility","precision","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.channel_aggression"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ef3ec55015c60bda"}}},{"_id":"f005336c552ac70c","name":"Equilibrium","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Adept","prerequisites":"","benefit":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Force Adept","treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","defender","force","shields","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.equilibrium"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.328a880e60f2320f"}}},{"_id":"4df2da8441e1de40","name":"Force Recovery","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":"Equilibrium, Second Wind","benefit":"When you use Second Wind, gain additional hit points: 1d6 per Force Point possessed (maximum 10d6).","description":"When you use Second Wind, gain additional hit points per Force Point you possess.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.equilibrium"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["feat-chain","force","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f8f445aa-d5a2-46b1-b832-c97039ae43fb","name":"Force Recovery","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.hp.regen","mode":2,"value":"1d6_per_fp"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Recovery"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_recovery"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a691cc0212b6176c"}}},{"_id":"dd11beb883835c24","name":"Indomitable Will","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Immune to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","description":"Gain immunity to all mind-affecting effects for 1 minute.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.indomitable_will"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a1f7a6ee66410c3e"}}},{"_id":"3696ef91564d240f","name":"Insight of the Force","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Archivist","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Use the Force replaces Knowledge when untrained and is treated as trained.","description":"Use the Force replaces Knowledge skills if untrained; you are considered trained.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Archivist","treeId":"152047d6ab7896ad","tags":["force","jedi","light-side","skills"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.insight_of_the_force"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.0adc25cfaa35147a"}}},{"_id":"9ece36f38342c6d8","name":"Mystical Link","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Adept","tree":"Force Adept","prerequisites":"","description":"When using the Telepathy ability of Use the Force, you reduce the DC of the Use the Force check by half, as do those Force-users for whom you are a willing telepathic recipient. When attempting to contact an unwilling target, you can reroll and take the better result. By spending a Force Point, you can simultaneously contact a number of targets equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum two) with a single Use the Force check. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions The Force guides you in unexpected ways. As a Standard Action, make a DC 30 Use the Force check. If the check is successful, you gain one of the following benefits, as selected by the Gamemaster: One Force Power is returned to your Force Power Suite. Gain one Force Point that is lost if it is not spent before the end of the encounter. Gain an additional use of a Force-related Talent or Feat normally restricted to once per encounter. Roll an additional die when making a Use the Force check and select the highest die rolled. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","benefit":"When using the Telepathy ability of Use the Force, you reduce the DC of the Use the Force check by half, as do those Force-users for whom you are a willing telepathic recipient. When attempting to contact an unwilling target, you can reroll and take the better result. By spending a Force Point, you can simultaneously contact a number of targets equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum two) with a single Use the Force check. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions The Force guides you in unexpected ways. As a Standard Action, make a DC 30 Use the Force check. If the check is successful, you gain one of the following benefits, as selected by the Gamemaster: One Force Power is returned to your Force Power Suite. Gain one Force Point that is lost if it is not spent before the end of the encounter. Gain an additional use of a Force-related Talent or Feat normally restricted to once per encounter. Roll an additional die when making a Use the Force check and select the highest die rolled. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","force","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.45c4e72d74c44acb"}}},{"_id":"d39ca32bd8f70ea6","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"05fbc3c4c513d83b","name":"Cloak","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Cloak"}}},{"_id":"c6e3e455e3cd9f5d","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"51a724bb169e46d8","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"d9ee86070f50d7fc","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","lightning"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0a422b939edfad56"}}},{"_id":"ed087e235f93892b","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"b4095b3d6d137bb5","name":"Ionize","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Ionize"}}},{"_id":"5febcb3c826ffb0a","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"ac3fd80c148cea06","name":"Negate Energy","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Reaction","range":"Personal or touch","target":"You or one creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use the Force to absorb or deflect energy damage. The target gains energy resistance 20 against one energy attack.</p>","special":"<p>This power can be used as a Reaction when you or an ally is targeted by an energy attack.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["defense","energy-resistance","protection"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.be1ae263c498af3b"}}},{"_id":"b3d16168ea189e08","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+5","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":13,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"6676f7512296126a","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+5","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":14,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"0d5ce512c3137a0c","name":"Blaster Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d6+6","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":1,"cost":500,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The standard sidearm used throughout the galaxy. Reliable, common, and effective at close to medium range.</p>","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"ranged","proficiency":"pistols","subcategory":"pistol","costNumeric":500,"category":"pistol"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-blaster-pistol"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":13,"flatDamageFormula":"3d6+6","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Medium","Species":"Human","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Medium Human Jedi":5,"Scoundrel":3,"Force Adept":3,"Jedi Knight":1},"Force Points":6,"Dark Side Points":5,"Languages":["Basic","Huttese"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":27,"Flat-Footed Defense":24,"Fortitude Defense":25,"Will Defense":28,"Hit Points":"104","Damage Threshold":25,"Speed":"6 Squares","Melee Weapons":"Unarmed +13 (1d4+5), Lightsaber +14 (2d8+5)","Ranged Weapons":"Blaster Pistol +13 (3d6+6)","Attack Options":["Unarmed","Lightsaber","Blaster Pistol"],"Force Powers":["Cloak","Farseeing","Force Grip","Force Lightning","Force Thrust","Ionize","Mind Trick","Negate Energy","Negate Energy"],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":["Improved Cloak"],"Strength":"8","Dexterity":"16","Constitution":"12","Intelligence":"12","Wisdom":"14","Charisma":"16","Talents":["Adept Negotiator","Channel Aggression","Equilibrium","Force Recovery","Indomitable Will","Insight of the Force","Mystical Link","Sneak Attack","(+1d6)"],"Feats":["Dodge","Force Readiness","Force Sensitivity","Force Training","(3)","Recovering Surge","Running Attack","Skill Focus (Use the Force)","Weapon Finesse","Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"],"Trained Skills":["Deception","Initiative","Perception","Use the Force"],"Gear":"Blaster Pistol , Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Jedi Robes H- Human bonus Feat or Trained Skill","Melee Attack":"","Ranged Attack":"","Species Bonuses":["Human\nbonus\nFeat","Attack Bonus"]},"mode":"play","sourcePack":"nonheroic","sourceAuthority":"statblock","playReady":true,"normalizedForPlay":true,"playNormalizationVersion":1,"statblockAuthority":true,"normalizationVersion":2,"nonheroicLegalSkeletonVersion":1,"nonheroicLegalSkeletonStatus":"heroic-profile"}}}}
