purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"2ae7cee45157e42d","name":"Devastating Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Weapon Master","prerequisites":"","benefit":"This replaces the effects of the Talent.","description":"This replaces the effects of the Talent.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Weapon Master","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["soldier"]},"effects":[{"_id":"69f7a1a0-603e-4b5e-a42a-15f770230266","name":"Devastating Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.combat.weaponGroupThresholdReduction","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Devastating Attack","effectType":"threshold_reduction","weaponGroupSpecific":true,"notes":"Weapon group specific - applies when using designated weapon group"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.devastating_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.383915a7d11e1225"}}},{"_id":"01de326346297ee9","name":"Elusive Dogfighter","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":"Wisdom 13","benefit":"You are an expert at escaping Dogfights. When making an opposed check to Disengage from a Dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the Dogfight, but the Gunners on your Vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per encounter, if your Vehicle takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied Vehicle. If your check result is higher, the allied Vehicle takes the damage instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Choose a single type of Vehicle from the following list: Airspeeder Capital Ship Space Transport Speeder Starfighter Walker When you are the Pilot or Gunner of that type of Vehicle, you gain a +2 bonus to all attack rolls with its Vehicle Weapons, and may Take 10 on any Pilot checks made while piloting that type of Vehicle, even when you are otherwise unable to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy As a Swift Action, you can make a DC 15 Pilot check to assist any allied Starfighter or Airspeeder within 2 squares at Starship Scale. If you succeed, the Pilot of that Vehicle gains a +5 bonus on all opposed Pilot checks relating to the Dogfight Action until the start of your next turn.","description":"You are an expert at escaping Dogfights. When making an opposed check to Disengage from a Dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the Dogfight, but the Gunners on your Vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per encounter, if your Vehicle takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied Vehicle. If your check result is higher, the allied Vehicle takes the damage instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Choose a single type of Vehicle from the following list: Airspeeder Capital Ship Space Transport Speeder Starfighter Walker When you are the Pilot or Gunner of that type of Vehicle, you gain a +2 bonus to all attack rolls with its Vehicle Weapons, and may Take 10 on any Pilot checks made while piloting that type of Vehicle, even when you are otherwise unable to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy As a Swift Action, you can make a DC 15 Pilot check to assist any allied Starfighter or Airspeeder within 2 squares at Starship Scale. If you succeed, the Pilot of that Vehicle gains a +5 bonus on all opposed Pilot checks relating to the Dogfight Action until the start of your next turn.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Expert Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["action-economy","defender","feat-chain","mobility","piloting","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.elusive_dogfighter"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fead6e3522fd458a"}}},{"_id":"8cafb87085feac6b","name":"Penetrating Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Weapon Master","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Chosen Weapon)","benefit":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","description":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Weapon Master","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["feat-chain","leader","scaling","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a0fba2f5-3da6-476e-9ac5-900be2d16e6b","name":"Penetrating Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.combat.weaponGroupDRReduction","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Penetrating Attack","effectType":"dr_reduction","weaponGroupSpecific":true,"notes":"Weapon group specific - applies when using designated weapon group"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.penetrating_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7d547902b8d9109e"}}},{"_id":"e22ce13cfce6a477","name":"Weapon Specialization","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Combat","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus","benefit":"+2 melee damage.","description":"Gain +2 damage with a chosen weapon.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Combat","treeId":"2359c05ff13f3feb","tags":["feat-chain","jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort"